@Lei-010 This is a genuinely useful addition — thank you. The failure point you isolated (the **autotune-group collective**, `_sync_oom_across_tune_group` -> `all_reduce` timeout) explains a detail our own writeup had flattened into "autotune pathologically slow": it is not slow, it is a hang shaped like slowness, and it is collective-shaped, which is why all 8 ranks show identical stacks and why the window burns to zero with no tokens. That strengthens the refusal case: this is not a "slow but working" backend that users could wait out.

On the 0.7.2 offer — yes, that would close the last open caveat, and it is exactly one window: on 0.7.2 the autotune path is fast (we measured ~1s per mxfp8 shape tier on the 84 GB 6000D with warm caches), so the failure character **changes** — serving comes up, and the arithmetic probes come back silently wrong (garbled output with zero engine errors, `temperature=0`). That transition from "hang before serving" to "serving with silent corruption" is the strongest form of the argument for refusing at startup rather than warning: the risk window does not close on 0.7.2, it moves.

If you do run it: `--moe-backend flashinfer_cutlass` on your Max-Q, a few deterministic arithmetic probes at `temperature=0` after READY is the whole test. Either outcome (hang persists on 97.9 GB, or serves-but-corrupts) is publishable as a datapoint here — no need for the full matrix.

